id: templates/mental-model
title: "Mental model template (questions first)"
kind: template
status: draft-0.1
spec_version: mental-model.v0.1
updated: 2026-09-09

purpose: >
  One formula for a mental model a principal can hand to a person or a bot.
  A mental model is a "why" made inspectable: what this is, why it matters
  from whose perspective, what is inside it, what to show, what was assumed,
  and what reality would have to show. The questions come first; the answers
  are attributed; unknowns stay lacunae.

communication_rule: >
  Talk at the level of the model, not the surface sentence. "I want money
  from you" is a sentence; "why do you want money from me, and did you even
  say it or did I infer it" is the model. Every page that uses this shape
  makes the why, the perspective, and the inference status visible before it
  asserts anything.

question_order_rule: >
  Ranked order is a View choice; question keys are stable. `role` (what am I
  to be here) is first. `relevance` (why do I need to know this) is next,
  and stays visible even when it is not asked out loud.

question_keys:
  - key: role
    prompt: "What am I to be here?"
    maps_to: perspective
  - key: relevance
    prompt: "Why do I need to know this?"
    maps_to: intent
  - key: definition
    prompt: "What is it?"
    maps_to: scope
  - key: inside
    prompt: "What is inside it?"
    maps_to: scope
  - key: show
    prompt: "What do I show?"
    maps_to: movement
  - key: assumptions
    prompt: "What am I assuming?"
    maps_to: current-state
  - key: proof
    prompt: "What would reality show me?"
    maps_to: proof
  - key: lacuna
    prompt: "What is still unknown?"
    maps_to: lacuna

shape:
  id: mental-model:<principal>:<slug>
  kind: mental-model
  principal_ref: principal:<name>
  arena: "<where this model is used>"
  questions:
    - key: role
      answer: "<one or two lines>"
  concept:
    name: "<name>"
    one_line: "<the model in one sentence>"
    inside:
      - name: "<part>"
        glyph: "<small mark a child could read>"
        one_line: "<what it is>"
  show:
    - icon: "<object or gesture>"
      do: "<what to do>"
      say: "<what to say, as a question>"
  embody:
    - "<how a person or bot carries this in their communication style>"
  assumptions:
    - text: "<assumption>"
      epistemic_status: assumed
  proof:
    signals:
      - "<what reality shows when it is working>"
    falsifier: "<what would show it is not working>"
  lacunae:
    - "<what stays unknown until observed>"
  sources:
    - text: "<named source>"
      epistemic_status: reported

projection_rule: >
  The .yawn record is the source. An HTML page under dave/<slug>/ is a View
  of it, uses only assets/site.css tokens, carries data-model and data-q
  markers in the record's question order, and is checked by
  scripts/validate-mental-models.mjs.
